---
import DocumentLayout from "../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro";
import {
  contactEmail,
  repositoryURL,
  threatModelURL,
} from "../data/site";

const effectiveDate = "7 November 2026";
---

<DocumentLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Sealbreak"
  description="How the Sealbreak iPhone app and the sealbreak.app website handle your data. The app collects no data and connects only to the server you configure."
  eyebrow="PRIVACY POLICY"
  heading="Sealbreak collects no data."
>
  <p slot="lead">
    Effective {effectiveDate}. This policy covers the Sealbreak iOS app and the
    website at sealbreak.app.
  </p>

  <h2>Summary</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The Sealbreak app does not collect, sell, or share any personal data.</li>
    <li>
      The app connects only to the OpenBao or HashiCorp Vault endpoint you
      configure. There is no Sealbreak server or relay.
    </li>
    <li>
      Your unseal share stays in the iOS Keychain on your iPhone. It is
      released only after Face ID, and only to send it to your server.
    </li>
    <li>
      The app contains no analytics, advertising, tracking, or crash-reporting
      SDKs.
    </li>
    <li>The website sets no cookies and runs no analytics or tracking.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    Sealbreak is developed by Georges Alkhouri as an independent open-source
    project. For any privacy question, write to{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The Sealbreak app</h2>

  <h3>Data stored on your iPhone</h3>
  <p>Sealbreak stores the following only on your device:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your Shamir unseal share.</strong> It is kept in the iOS
      Keychain, bound to this device, protected by Face ID, and excluded from
      iCloud Keychain sync. Sealbreak offers no way to export it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Server settings</strong>, such as the server name and HTTPS
      address you enter. They are stored in the app's protected storage and
      excluded from device backups.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    None of this is sent to the developer. Deleting the app or resetting it in
    the app removes it from your iPhone.
  </p>

  <h3>Face ID</h3>
  <p>
    Face ID is handled entirely by iOS. Sealbreak only receives a yes or no
    from the system and never has access to your face data.
  </p>

  <h3>Clipboard</h3>
  <p>
    Sealbreak reads the clipboard only when you tap paste to import a share.
    After a valid share is pasted, Sealbreak clears the clipboard.
  </p>

  <h3>Network connections</h3>
  <p>
    Sealbreak connects only to the server address you configure, and only over
    HTTPS with normal certificate validation. It sends status requests and,
    after you approve with Face ID, your unseal share. This traffic goes
    directly from your iPhone to your server, or to a TLS proxy you run in
    front of it. The developer has no access to it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Sealbreak does not use cookies, caches, or stored credentials for these
    connections. What your server logs is controlled by you, not by
    Sealbreak.
  </p>

  <h3>Analytics, tracking, and crash reports</h3>
  <p>
    The app contains no analytics, advertising, tracking, or crash-reporting
    SDKs, and it does not track you across apps or websites. Its App Store
    privacy manifest declares no tracking and no collected data types.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you have turned on <em>Share With App Developers</em> in iOS settings,
    Apple may give the developer anonymous crash reports and usage statistics.
    This sharing is optional and governed by{" "}
    <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's privacy policy</a>.
    If you join the TestFlight beta, Apple's TestFlight terms apply to the
    feedback and crash reports you choose to send.
  </p>

  <h2>The sealbreak.app website</h2>
  <p>
    The website is a static site hosted by Cloudflare. It sets no cookies, uses
    no analytics or tracking, and loads no third-party scripts, fonts, or
    embeds.
  </p>
  <p>
    To deliver and protect the site, Cloudflare processes technical request
    data such as your IP address, browser user agent, and the page requested.
    Cloudflare may keep this data in short-lived logs. This processing is
    covered by{" "}
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
    The developer does not use it to identify or profile visitors.
    Cloudflare may process this data in the United States and other countries
    outside the EU. Cloudflare is certified under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy
    Framework, which covers these transfers.
  </p>
  <p>
    Links to GitHub, TestFlight, and the App Store lead to services with their
    own privacy policies.
  </p>

  <h2>When you contact us</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us or open a GitHub issue, we use what you send only to answer
    you and improve Sealbreak. Emails are not shared with third parties. GitHub
    issues are public and governed by{" "}
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
    Please never include an unseal share, root token, or other secret in a
    message or issue.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Because the app collects no data, the developer holds no app data about
    you. For any email you have sent, you can ask for access, correction, or
    deletion at{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. You may also lodge a
    complaint with your data protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the updated version will be published on this page
    with a new effective date. The source of the app and this website is
    public, so you can check every change.
  </p>

  <p class="muted">
    More detail on how Sealbreak protects your share is in the{" "}
    <a href={threatModelURL}>threat model</a> and the{" "}
    <a href={repositoryURL}>source code</a>.
  </p>
</DocumentLayout>
